# Scenario "staff-credits" (PAL, milestones 6 and 9, issues 1 and 5): the staff-credits THP movie (50 Hz: the 25 fps
# file), reached without an advanced save. The stage 10 script plays the movie as soon as the stage starts, with no
# condition, so it is enough to load any save into stage 10: tools/run.py --stage staff-credit replaces the stage
# stored in the save once, at the restore (game.toml, [stage]). 60/50 Hz prompt (50 Hz) -> title screen -> Load Game
# -> file 1 -> the movie (about 116 s) -> the game goes back to the player's home stage (next morning).
# Run it with the user folder left by the "new-game" scenario (save in slot 1, dated at the bench clock):
#   py -3 tools/run.py chibi-robo --version GGTP01 --stage staff-credit --user-seed <new-game folder>/user \
#     --scenario games/chibi-robo/scenarios/play/GGTP01/staff-credits.scn
# Checkpoints: every 10 frames around the start and the end of the movie, every 60 frames in between (the VI
# field of each checkpoint gives the cadence), 30 consecutive frames in the middle (each frame of the movie is shown).
# Not run by tools/ab.py (progression scenario). No game data here: buttons, frame numbers and names only.
# Recorded on GGTP01 (cycle clock, RTC 800000000).
name staff-credits
description The new-game save loaded into stage 10 (--stage staff-credit): the staff-credits THP movie, then back to the game (PAL).
version GGTP01
after new-game     # preparation: user folder (save) left by "new-game"
window 0
input  150 A       # 60/50 Hz prompt: confirm the 50 Hz option
input 1050 A       # health and safety warning
input 2600 A       # title screen: Load Game
input 2850 LEFT    # Load Game file selection: from file 1 to file 3 (the cursor wraps around)
input 2900 RIGHT   # ... and back to file 1
input 2950 A       # load file 1
check 2940 file-1-selected
